      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Size left unknown: NC State (10 to 30 ft) and RHS (4 to 8 m) give outdoor or wild sizes, and both say indoor plants stay smaller. Temperature is a minimum only (RHS: keep above about 15 C). NC State rates the plant low severity for people and notes the palm heart contains cyanide-releasing compounds; not graded here. Look-alikes come from the look-alike list (knowledge, verify). Interval: NC State 'keep moist but not soggy during the growing season'; Missouri Botanical Garden 'consistent moisture' for houseplants; RHS keep moist. Three sources agree on moist, none gives a depth, so 7 days for a 13 cm pot stays unconfirmed. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, growing season; winter comes from the rest-season factor. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives any, unchanged."
      },
